# Agent Tool Development Patterns

## Overview
This rule defines the standard patterns for developing tools for the Juno AI Computer Use Agent, based on the successful accessibility tools implementation.

## Tool Architecture Pattern

### Core Structure
Every agent tool should follow this modular structure:
1. **Tool Implementation**: Core logic in `src-tauri/src/agent/tools/{tool_name}.rs`
2. **Tauri Commands**: Frontend interface in `src-tauri/src/commands/{tool_name}.rs`
3. **Registration**: Integration in [factory.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/providers/factory.rs)
4. **Mapping**: Categorization in [tool_mapping.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/tools/tool_mapping.rs)

### Tool Implementation Template
```rust
#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct YourTools {
    // Use Arc<Mutex<>> for thread-safe shared state
    state: Arc<Mutex<YourState>>,
    cache: Arc<Mutex<HashMap<String, CachedData>>>,
}

impl YourTools {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            state: Arc::new(Mutex::new(YourState::default())),
            cache: Arc::new(Mutex::new(HashMap::new())),
        }
    }

    // Tool definition method (required)
    pub fn get_tool_definitions() -> Vec<Value> {
        vec![
            json!({
                "name": "your_tool",
                "description": "Description of what your tool does",
                "input_schema": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "param": {"type": "string", "description": "Parameter description"}
                    },
                    "required": ["param"]
                }
            })
        ]
    }

    // Tool executor method (required)
    pub async fn execute_tool(&self, tool_name: &str, parameters: &Value, app_handle: &AppHandle) -> Result<Value, String> {
        match tool_name {
            "your_tool" => self.your_tool_impl(parameters, app_handle).await,
            _ => Err(format!("Unknown tool: {}", tool_name))
        }
    }

    // Individual tool implementations
    async fn your_tool_impl(&self, parameters: &Value, _app_handle: &AppHandle) -> Result<Value, String> {
        // Implementation here
        Ok(json!({"success": true}))
    }
}
```

## Tauri Commands Pattern

### Command File Template (`src-tauri/src/commands/{tool_name}.rs`)
```rust
use crate::agent::tools::{YourTools, YourDataType};
use serde_json::Value;
use std::sync::Mutex;
use tracing::{debug, info};

// Global tool instance
lazy_static::lazy_static! {
    static ref YOUR_TOOLS: Mutex<YourTools> = Mutex::new(YourTools::new());
}

/// Primary tool command
#[tauri::command]
pub async fn your_primary_command(param: String) -> Result<YourDataType, String> {
    debug!("your_primary_command called with: {}", param);

    let tools = YOUR_TOOLS.lock().map_err(|e| format!("Lock error: {}", e))?;
    let result = tools.your_method(param)?;

    info!("your_primary_command completed successfully");
    Ok(result)
}

/// Generic tool executor for agent use
#[tauri::command]
pub async fn execute_your_tool(
    tool_name: String,
    parameters: Value,
    app_handle: tauri::AppHandle,
) -> Result<Value, String> {
    debug!("execute_your_tool called: {}", tool_name);

    // Clone to avoid holding lock across await
    let tools = {
        let tools_guard = YOUR_TOOLS.lock().map_err(|e| format!("Lock error: {}", e))?;
        tools_guard.clone()
    };

    let result = tools.execute_tool(&tool_name, &parameters, &app_handle).await?;
    info!("execute_your_tool completed: {}", tool_name);
    Ok(result)
}

/// Tool definitions for agent discovery
#[tauri::command]
pub async fn get_your_tool_definitions() -> Result<Vec<Value>, String> {
    Ok(YourTools::get_tool_definitions())
}
```

## Registration Pattern

### Factory Registration ([factory.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/providers/factory.rs))
```rust
/// Register your tools for element-level interaction
pub async fn register_your_tools(
    provider: &mut LocalToolProvider,
    app_handle: tauri::AppHandle,
) -> Result<(), String> {
    info!("🔧 Registering your tools...");

    let your_tools = YourTools::new();
    let tool_definitions = YourTools::get_tool_definitions();

    for tool_def in tool_definitions {
        let tool_name = tool_def["name"].as_str().unwrap_or("unknown").to_string();
        let description = tool_def["description"].as_str().unwrap_or("").to_string();
        let input_schema = tool_def["input_schema"].clone();

        let tool_definition = crate::agent::core::ToolDefinition {
            name: tool_name.clone(),
            description,
            input_schema,
        };

        let tools_clone = your_tools.clone();
        let app_handle_clone = app_handle.clone();
        let tool_name_clone = tool_name.clone();

        let executor = move |input: serde_json::Value| {
            let tools = tools_clone.clone();
            let app = app_handle_clone.clone();
            let name = tool_name_clone.clone();

            async move {
                tools.execute_tool(&name, &input, &app).await
            }
        };

        provider.register_async_tool(tool_definition, executor).await;
    }

    info!("🔧 Your tools registered successfully");
    Ok(())
}
```

Add to `register_computer_use_tools()`:
```rust
// Register your tools
Self::register_your_tools(provider, app_handle.clone()).await?;
```

## Module Integration Pattern

### Module Declaration ([mod.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/tools/mod.rs))
```rust
pub mod your_tools; // Add your module
pub use your_tools::{YourTools, YourDataType}; // Export types
```

### Command Exports ([commands/mod.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/commands/mod.rs))
```rust
pub mod your_tool_commands; // Declare module

// Re-export commands
pub use self::your_tool_commands::{
    your_primary_command, execute_your_tool, get_your_tool_definitions
};
```

### Command Registration ([lib.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/lib.rs))
Add to imports:
```rust
use commands::{
    your_primary_command, execute_your_tool, get_your_tool_definitions,
    // ... other imports
};
```

Add to `tauri::generate_handler!`:
```rust
your_primary_command,
execute_your_tool,
get_your_tool_definitions,
```

